text.section:
The partnership agreement may not:

Vary the rights and duties in § 50-73.83 except to eliminate the duty to provide copies of statements to all of the partners;


Unreasonably restrict the right of access to books and records in subsection B of § 50-73.101;


Eliminate the obligation of good faith and fair dealing in subsection D of § 50-73.102, but the partnership agreement may prescribe the standards by which the performance of the obligation is to be measured, if the standards are not manifestly unreasonable;


Vary the power to dissociate as a partner in subsection A of § 50-73.110, except to require the notice in subdivision 1 of § 50-73.109 to be in writing;


Vary the right of a court to expel a partner in the events specified in subdivision 5 of § 50-73.109;


Vary the requirement to wind up the partnership business in cases specified in subdivisions 4, 5 or 6 of § 50-73.117;


Restrict rights of third parties under this chapter without the consent of those third parties; or


Vary the law applicable to registered limited liability partnerships as set forth in subsection B of § 50-73.84.
